    {
      "heading": "A new leader",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "person-yi-chia-chen-identity-0"
      ],
      "text": "Yi-Chia Chen @ Fields Model leads the ARC-AGI-3 public board at the Late edition close, putting Tufa Labs in second. The saved score event records Chen rising from 68.21 to 71.48 and moving from second to first. That leaves a 2.57-point lead over Tufa’s unchanged 68.91. The board lists threerabbits for Chen’s entry; the result belongs to this contest and does not alter the separate ARC-AGI-2 standings."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The chase behind them",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board"
      ],
      "text": "Team Turducken holds third at 56.02 without another score increase since the previous close. The last dance reaches 50.69 and fourth place: its recorded score event is an advance from 49.85, enough to move ahead of mtg at 50.37. NVARC3 remains eighth at 45.90, with artificialagencylab.com ninth and Majkel1337 tenth. Chen’s lead change and the reshuffle behind third give the day its consequence; the rest of that leading group has not posted a new net gain in the edition’s comparison."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Progress still has to beat the field",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-25-1557-arc-3-kubo-kan-climbs-to-78th"
      ],
      "text": "Jan Disselhoff improves by 0.21 to 38.58 but closes eighteenth, one place below the previous close, as the provisional gold score rises from 38.20 to 38.22. Lord Han Solo is twenty-ninth at an unchanged 37.07. Further down, menphim gains 1.29 to reach 34.31 and sixty-seventh, up eighty-eight places. The afternoon wire also reports 久保兼 reaching 33.98 and seventy-eighth from a four-digit rank; that is the wire’s dated observation, rather than a new improvement after its report."
    },
    {
      "heading": "What this edition can establish",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board"
      ],
      "text": "Public positions and medal bands remain provisional. Social and discussion research was not refreshed for this edition. The October 22 participant report about scoring problems has no confirmed follow-up in the saved evidence used here; today’s board movements do not establish its scope, cause or resolution."
